 /*
- * Pixel 3 (blueline) touchscreen: ST FTS ("st,fts" at I2C 0x49) on the
- * GENI I2C engine QUP wrapper 0 / SE2 (i2c@888000), polled every 10 ms,
- * contacts passed to the HID services (iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp)
- * in panel pixels (1080x2160).
+ * Pixel 3 (blueline) touchscreen: ST FTM5 ("st,fts", chip id 36 39) at I2C
+ * 0x49, contacts passed to the HID services (iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/SweetHID.cpp)
+ * in panel pixels (1080x2160). Shown working by the p3-input probe first.
  *
- * Off by default until the p3-input probe has shown the chip answering:
- * boot-arg bluetouch=1 turns it on. Writes: GCC clock votes for wrapper 0
- * AHB and SE2 plus the SE2 clock source (crystal), the TLMM mux of GPIO
- * 27/28 to qup2, and the serial engine's registers. The chip only gets
- * read commands (no reset, no power or scan-mode changes): it must already
- * be sensing.
+ * The bus: i2c@888000 (QUP wrapper 0, SE2) has its FIFO interface disabled,
+ * and its GPI DMA path takes the SoC down on the first descriptor fetch, so
+ * the bus is bit-banged on the SE's own pins (as HackiOS drives its panel's
+ * SPI): GPIO 27 SDA, 28 SCL, open drain by switching the output enable with
+ * the output held low, pull-ups on, ~100 kHz, interrupts masked during each
+ * transfer. GPIO 136 (st,switch_gpio) high gives the bus to us, not the
+ * sensor hub.
  *
- * FTS event FIFO (command 0x86, 8-byte events, byte 7 bits 4:0 = events
- * still queued): byte 0 high nibble 1 enter, 2 motion, 3 leave; byte 1 =
- * id << 4 | type (1 finger); x = (b3 & 0xf) << 8 | b2, y = b4 << 4 | b3 >> 4.
+ * Power: avdd-supply is PM8998 LDO19 (3.3 V), owned by the AOP and off after
+ * the bootloader; the chip then answers and scans but never sees a finger.
+ * It is asked for over RPMh as Linux does (cmd-db.c, rpmh-rsc.c,
+ * qcom-rpmh-regulator.c): "ldoa19" looked up in the AOP's command database,
+ * then voltage, mode HPM and enable in one active TCS of the apps RSC (DRV 2).
+ *
+ * Start-up as Google's driver resumes the chip (stm/fts.c fts_resume_work):
+ * system reset (0x20000024 = 0x80), wait for "controller ready" (0x03),
+ * interrupt enable (0x20000029 = 0x41), scan mode active with every scan the
+ * config supports (A0 00 FF).
+ *
+ * Events (command 0x86, 8 bytes each, byte 7 bits 4:0 = events still queued):
+ * byte 0 high nibble 1 enter, 2 motion, 3 leave; byte 1 = id << 4 | type
+ * (1 finger); x = (b3 & 0xf) << 8 | b2, y = b4 << 4 | b3 >> 4. Read while
+ * the IRQ line (GPIO 125, active low) says events are pending, and every
+ * 100 ms regardless. Boot-arg bluetouch=0 turns all of this off.
  */
